    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d828">

                <pb facs="0878" n="779" xml:id="pg779"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">852.1115/2385: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Third Secretary of Embassy in Spain</hi>
                        (<hi rendition="#italic">Wendelin</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener>
                    <dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Madrid</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1936-11-26T09:00:00+00:00">November 26, 1936—9
                        a.m.</date><lb/>[Received 11:40 a.m.]</dateline>
                </opener>
                <p>X–358. First party about 55 people with last minute additions left for Valencia
                    in charge of Consul Johnson and Colonel Fuqua 7:15 this morning. Departure
                    delayed by necessity of sending car to pick up two Americans in outlying
                    section. Weather cloudy and rainy making danger from aeroplanes slight.<anchor
                        n="6" xml:id="d828-f1"/></p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Wendelin</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d828-f1" n="6" xml:id="d828-f1-content">
                <p>The Third Secretary of Embassy in Spain reported in a telegram filed about 1:45
                    p.m. that he was leaving within the hour, accompanied by officials of the
                    telephone company (124.52/149, 160).</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
